.TH UPDATE\-EVERY\-THING 1 "2026" "update-every-thing @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
update\-every\-thing \- run every Fedora update in one pass
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B update\-every\-thing
[\fB\-c\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-with\-nvidia\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the updates a Fedora desktop needs, in an order that only refreshes
repository metadata once, and prints a summary of what happened at the end.
.PP
The steps are:
.IP 1. 4
Antigravity IDE, via
.BR antigravity\-update (1)
if it is installed.
.IP 2. 4
System packages, with the run's single
.B dnf
metadata refresh.
.IP 3. 4
Firmware, through
.BR fwupdmgr (1).
.IP 4. 4
Flatpak applications.
.IP 5. 4
GNOME extensions \(em listed only. The RPM\-packaged ones were already
upgraded in step 2, and running dnf again for them just re\-downloads every
repository to print "Nothing to do".
.IP 6. 4
Cleanup:
.B dnf autoremove
and
.BR "dnf clean all" .
.PP
Nothing aborts the run. A step that fails is retried a bounded number of times
and then given up on, so the run always reaches the end and you get one report
instead of discovering a failure three commands later. A step whose tool is not
installed is skipped and recorded as such.
.PP
Neither stdout nor stderr is redirected. That is deliberate: dnf and flatpak
draw progress on stderr and size it from the terminal, so piping either stream
costs them the terminal and their progress bars come out duplicated and
wrapped.
.PP
The sudo timestamp is refreshed in the background for the length of the run, so
no password prompt appears in the middle of a long download.
.PP
Ctrl\-C stops the run and still prints the summary, marking the step that was
running as interrupted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-retries " " \fIN\fR
Attempt each failing step up to \fIN\fR times before giving up on it and moving
to the next. Default \fB5\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-with\-nvidia
Update NVIDIA and CUDA packages too. They are excluded by default because
replacing the driver under a running session can break it.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every step that ran succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
At least one step failed.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with Ctrl\-C.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.EX
update\-every\-thing
update\-every\-thing \-c 3
update\-every\-thing \-\-with\-nvidia
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dnf (8),
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR fwupdmgr (1),
.BR antigravity\-update (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @MAINTAINER@.
